1
00:00:06,095 --> 00:00:08,447
Whiskers and the Chimney Cake.

2
00:00:18,024 --> 00:00:22,124
One snowy night, the cats were warming their paws by the fire.

3
00:00:28,418 --> 00:00:31,125
Hey! Who is throwing logs down the chimney?

4
00:00:35,544 --> 00:00:38,979
Ahoj! I'm Kasparek, a puppet from Prague! The wind blew me here!

5
00:00:39,179 --> 00:00:40,582
But who pulls your strings?

6
00:00:40,782 --> 00:00:43,279
Nobody! It's Christmas magic. But look. Knots!

7
00:00:46,761 --> 00:00:49,323
Tiny knots need tiny paws. Hold still!

8
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:58,020
Thank you! Now I must get home. When the old clock strikes twelve,

9
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:00,096
and our Christmas puppet show begins!

10
00:01:00,296 --> 00:01:03,701
The Astronomical Clock! Little figures come out every hour!

11
00:01:03,901 --> 00:01:06,192
And a skeleton rings the bell. Ding, ding!

12
00:01:06,392 --> 00:01:08,869
A skeleton? I'm staying right here.

13
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:11,801
Pity. Prague has chimney cakes. Warm and sugary.

14
00:01:15,282 --> 00:01:16,808
Which way is Prague?

15
00:01:19,821 --> 00:01:25,181
So they hid on a barge full of Christmas trees, and floated down the river all night.

16
00:01:32,413 --> 00:01:35,437
It smells like a forest. With no snacks.

17
00:01:42,201 --> 00:01:44,689
Wake up! Prague! The castle, and a hundred spires!

18
00:01:44,889 --> 00:01:47,968
One spire, two spires... ninety-nine...

19
00:01:54,731 --> 00:01:59,478
They crossed the Charles Bridge, with its stone saints and street musicians.

20
00:02:07,179 --> 00:02:08,514
Hurry! It's almost noon!

21
00:02:12,464 --> 00:02:14,110
Sniff, sniff. Cinnamon!

22
00:02:18,998 --> 00:02:22,579
The Old Town Square glowed with Christmas lights.

23
00:02:27,467 --> 00:02:29,339
A chimney cake, for my rescuers!

24
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:39,722
Whiskers! You've got your head stuck in a chimney cake!

25
00:02:39,922 --> 00:02:42,176
I did that on purpose. It's a hat.

26
00:02:48,002 --> 00:02:50,504
Aaah! The skeleton! It looked at me!

27
00:02:53,517 --> 00:02:57,142
It was one minute to noon. And then, the clock stopped.

28
00:03:02,030 --> 00:03:05,683
Oh dear, oh dear. Something is stuck in my gears.

29
00:03:05,883 --> 00:03:10,918
If I can't ring my bell, the clock can't strike twelve. No puppet show!

30
00:03:11,118 --> 00:03:13,100
Whiskers... where is your chimney cake?

31
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:15,826
Oh no. It flew right into the clock.

32
00:03:16,026 --> 00:03:19,504
Someone must climb inside, through that little door.

33
00:03:19,704 --> 00:03:21,439
Up there? Right next to you?

34
00:03:21,639 --> 00:03:26,122
Don't be afraid, little cat. I'm only bones, and a big smile.

35
00:03:30,072 --> 00:03:32,507
That cake is my mess. I'll fix it.

36
00:03:39,739 --> 00:03:43,360
Inside was a giant maze of golden wheels.

37
00:03:48,248 --> 00:03:50,949
There it is. Stuck in the biggest wheel.

38
00:03:51,149 --> 00:03:53,750
This is the job I was born for.

39
00:04:07,545 --> 00:04:09,689
Delicious! The clock is free!

40
00:04:14,577 --> 00:04:19,264
The skeleton rang his bell, and the apostles marched past the windows.

41
00:04:26,965 --> 00:04:30,404
Thank you, brave cat. You saved twelve o'clock!

42
00:04:30,604 --> 00:04:34,249
You're not scary at all, Mister Bones. Just a bit thin.

43
00:04:34,449 --> 00:04:37,815
And you're not a scaredy cat. Just a bit round.

44
00:04:41,765 --> 00:04:43,677
And the puppet show began!

45
00:04:49,972 --> 00:04:52,951
The story of a brave cat, who ate his way into a clock!

46
00:05:00,183 --> 00:05:02,553
Come back soon, my friends! Na shledanou!

47
00:05:12,598 --> 00:05:16,202
The empty barge carried them home under the stars.

48
00:05:21,090 --> 00:05:22,989
You're back! Did you bring me anything?

49
00:05:23,189 --> 00:05:26,501
One chimney cake. I saved it just for you.

50
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:28,410
I only licked it a little.

51
00:05:28,610 --> 00:05:32,034
Merry Christmas, Luna. Don't wake me before noon.

52
00:05:32,234 --> 00:05:38,860
A friend can be wooden, or tiny, or made of bones. What matters is the kind heart inside.

